{
  "description": "Which layer stack a resolver must hook on a multi-tower (composite) model, shared by miWorkbench (producer) and miServer (consumer). A composite checkpoint (Gemma 3 and 4 ...ForConditionalGeneration, LLaVA, Qwen2.5-VL) declares its vision tower before its text decoder, so a first-match search over the module tree hooks a vision encoder layer that a text forward never runs (ENH-011 #2). Every resolver must return the TEXT DECODER's layer list: the stack whose owning module also owns the model's input token embedding. Its depth must equal config.get_text_config(decoder=True).num_hidden_layers, and a mismatch is refused, never guessed. Each case names the transformers config and model classes, the dotted path of the text decoder's layer list (text_layers_path) and of the vision stack a first-match search would have taken (vision_layers_path, absent for a single-tower control), and tiny_config: the keyword arguments that build a CPU-sized copy with random weights, so both repos test the same models without downloading anything. text_depth is that tiny copy's text depth. Change a case HERE first, then both resolvers; miServer keeps a byte-identical copy.",
